# The starting menu, with nothing saved.
#
# **`spec/tests/interface/README.md`: *an interface test is written in the same form as a rule
# test... the `then` is the whole of what the interface shows.*** So two rows and nothing else
# means two items, and a third appearing makes this red.
#
# **No `displayed` column**, because an item is displayed by being here. **No order**, because the
# rows are a multiset - the known limitation that form records.
#
# **Sean, 2026-10-01**: *top menu items are continue, load, new game, exit.* With nothing saved,
# *continue* and *load* are not shown at all - which under this form is the same as their not being
# there.

{test name:the-starting-menu-offers-new-game-and-exit}

{given}
{saves} -> 0

{when}
{open-menu}

{then}
{item name:new-game active:1} -> 1
{item name:exit active:1} -> 1
{attention of:new-game}
